# Byte-exact files. Git's automatic CRLF↔LF normalisation would silently
# corrupt these, and the corruption would only show up as a mysterious parser
# test failure on a fresh clone.

# The MIME conformance corpus IS its bytes. RFC 822 line endings are CRLF, the
# header/body boundary is a blank CRLF line, and case 25 exists specifically to
# test a message with mixed CRLF and bare LF. Normalising any of that would turn
# the corpus into a test of something else.
*.eml           -text

# SSE fixtures are the exact wire bytes of a stream, blank-line framing included.
*.sse           -text

# Binaries, marked so git never inspects or rewrites them.
*.ttf           binary
*.png           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.sqlite3       binary
*.p8            binary

# Xcode's project file merges badly and should be reviewed as a whole.
*.pbxproj       -text merge=union linguist-generated
